---
import LegalLayout from "../layouts/LegalLayout.astro";
import { FOUNDING_ACTIVE, FOUNDING_ENDS_LABEL } from "../lib/pricing";

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, "");
---

<LegalLayout
  title="Terms & Conditions — CG Design & Co."
  description="The terms that apply when you work with CG Design & Co. on a website, branding or setup job, for businesses and individuals."
  pageTitle="Terms & Conditions"
  lastUpdated="20 November 2026"
>
  <h2>About us</h2>
  <p>
    CG Design &amp; Co. is a registered business name (ABN 25 672 082 550),
    based at St Luke Street, Randwick NSW 2031, Australia. You can reach us
    at <a href="mailto:info@cgdesignaus.com">info@cgdesignaus.com</a> or on
    <a href="https://wa.me/447306100251" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">WhatsApp (+44 7306 100251)</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Who these terms apply to</h2>
  <p>
    These terms apply whenever you ask us to design, build or maintain a
    website, or do branding or setup work ("the services"), whether you're
    a business or an individual. By accepting a quote or proposal from us,
    you accept these terms.
  </p>
  <p>
    Nothing in these terms takes away rights you have by law. If you're a
    consumer, that includes the consumer guarantees under the Australian
    Consumer Law and, if you live in the UK, your rights under the Consumer
    Rights Act 2015 and the Consumer Contracts Regulations 2013.
  </p>

  <h2>Prices and currency</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      All prices are in Australian dollars (AUD). We're not registered for
      GST, so no GST is added to our prices.
    </li>
    <li>
      If you pay from outside Australia, your bank or card provider may
      charge currency conversion fees. Those are set by them, not us.
    </li>
    <li>
      Before any work begins, we give you a fixed, written price based on
      the pages and features you choose. It won't change once agreed, unless
      you ask for extra pages or features partway through, and then we'll
      agree the extra cost with you first.
    </li>
    <li>
      Figures from the quote builder on this site are estimates until we
      confirm them in writing.
    </li>
    {FOUNDING_ACTIVE && (
      <li>
        Our founding client offer (half price on website packages) applies to
        quotes accepted by {FOUNDING_ENDS_LABEL}. The crossed-out prices on
        this site are our standard prices, which apply after that date.
      </li>
    )}
    <li>
      Your web address (domain name) is $49 a year. We register it in your
      name or your business's name and renew it each year while you're with
      us. The Complete package includes the first year.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Payment</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>We take payments by card through Stripe.</li>
    <li>For website projects, a 50% deposit is payable before work begins.</li>
    <li>The remaining 50% is due on completion, before the site goes live or files are handed over.</li>
    <li>Quick jobs and branding are paid in full before we start, unless we agree otherwise in writing.</li>
    <li>Any hosting &amp; care plan is billed on the 1st of every month.</li>
    <li>The hosting &amp; care plan includes up to 1 hour of content changes each month. Unused time doesn't roll over, and bigger changes are quoted before we start.</li>
    <li>Your web address is billed once a year, starting when it's registered. If you'd rather renew it yourself, we'll transfer it to you at any time.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>What we need from you</h2>
  <p>
    To keep your project on track, we need you to send content (text,
    images, logos) and feedback within a reasonable time when we ask for
    it. Delays on your side may delay the delivery date.
  </p>
  <p>
    By sending us content, you confirm you have the right to use it on your
    website, and you let us use it for that purpose.
  </p>

  <h2>Ownership</h2>
  <p>
    Once the final payment has been made, the website and, if we registered
    it for you, its domain name belong to you. Until then, the work remains
    ours.
  </p>
  <p>
    Some parts of a website come from third parties, such as fonts, stock
    photos, booking systems or payment tools. You can use them on your site
    under their own licences and terms.
  </p>
  <p>
    We may show non-confidential parts of the finished work in our
    portfolio unless you ask us not to.
  </p>

  <h2>Your right to cancel</h2>
  <p>
    <strong>Consumers in the UK or EU:</strong> you can cancel within 14
    days of accepting our quote, without giving a reason, by telling us in
    writing (email is fine). If you asked us to start work during those 14
    days, you'll pay for the work done up to the point you told us you were
    cancelling. If we've fully completed the work at your request within the
    14 days, the right to cancel no longer applies.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>Everyone:</strong> you can cancel a project at any time by
    telling us in writing. You'll pay for the work completed up to that
    point, and anything you've paid beyond that is refunded. See our
    <a href={`${base}/refund-policy/`}>Refund Policy</a> for details.
  </p>
  <p>
    You can cancel a hosting &amp; care plan at any time. You won't be
    charged again after your current month.
  </p>

  <h2>If something isn't right</h2>
  <p>
    We'll do the work with due care and skill, and fix anything we built
    that doesn't work as agreed at no extra cost. Our services come with
    guarantees that can't be excluded under the Australian Consumer Law and,
    for UK consumers, the Consumer Rights Act 2015. For a major failure,
    you're entitled to cancel and get a refund, or to compensation for the
    drop in value. You're also entitled to compensation for any other loss
    or damage that was reasonably foreseeable.
  </p>

  <h2>Liability</h2>
  <p>
    We can't guarantee specific business results (such as a particular
    amount of traffic, bookings or sales) from a website alone. We're not
    responsible for problems caused by things outside our reasonable
    control, such as outages at a hosting provider or a third-party service
    your site relies on.
  </p>
  <p>
    If you're a business customer, and as far as the law allows, our total
    liability for any project is limited to the amount you paid us for it,
    and we're not liable for indirect losses such as lost profits.
  </p>
  <p>
    Nothing in these terms excludes, restricts or changes any guarantee,
    right or remedy you have under the Australian Consumer Law or other
    consumer protection law that can't lawfully be excluded, or limits
    liability for death or personal injury caused by negligence, or for
    fraud.
  </p>

  <h2>Your personal data</h2>
  <p>
    We handle your personal data as described in our
    <a href={`${base}/privacy-policy/`}>Privacy Policy</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Governing law and disputes</h2>
  <p>
    If there's a problem, please tell us first and we'll do our best to sort
    it out. These terms are governed by the law of New South Wales,
    Australia, and the courts of New South Wales can hear any dispute.
  </p>
  <p>
    If you're a consumer living in the UK or EU, you also keep the
    protection of the mandatory laws of the country where you live, and you
    can bring a claim in your local courts.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes to these terms</h2>
  <p>
    We may update these terms from time to time. The date at the top shows
    when they last changed. A project already agreed in writing is covered
    by the terms in place when you accepted your quote.
  </p>
</LegalLayout>
